<template>
    <SiteShell page="about">
        <h1>About</h1>
        <p class="lead">
            OpenCleaner is a free, open-source disk cleaning tool built by
            the WAE project as its own daily-driver utility.
        </p>

        <section class="block">
            <h2>Why it exists</h2>
            <p>
                Commercial cleaners charge for what should be basic system
                hygiene, and many quietly collect usage data. OpenCleaner
                inverts that: the whole pipeline is local, the rules are
                auditable, and removal always goes through the Recycle Bin.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="block">
            <h2>The stack</h2>
            <p>
                The scanning and cleanup core is written in Rust. The
                desktop GUI is a native WebView surface built with the VMZ
                compiler, and the command-line interface is assembled on
                top of the WAE Commander toolkit. Everything ships under
                the Apache-2.0 license.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="block">
            <h2>Get involved</h2>
            <p>
                Rule packs, translations and platform fixes are welcome.
                Open an issue or a pull request on the public repository —
                or just run
                <Link to="DownloadPage">
                    OpenCleaner
                </Link>
                and tell us what it missed.
            </p>
        </section>
    </SiteShell>
</template>

